// ============================================================
// TODO BACKLOG — Core Framework Tasks
// Process: STRICT HOLD — do NOT implement any task until the
// backlog is declared complete. Then pick ONLY the first
// uncompleted task, implement it, write validation tests,
// mark it [x] here, and stop for review.
// ============================================================

// Phase 1: Editor & Code Quality
// [x] 1. More languages: Enable syntax highlighting for Python, JSON, CSS, Markdown, and TypeScript in addition to the existing JavaScript. Language auto-detects from file extension, with a manual override in the status bar or command palette.
// [x] 2. Live preview pane: Add a toggleable split-view render pane. When the active file is .html or .md, render it live (debounced ~300ms after typing stops): HTML in a sandboxed iframe, Markdown as styled HTML. Show a clear placeholder for non-previewable files.
// [x] 3. Multi-cursor editing: Enable multi-cursor editing: Ctrl+D selects the next occurrence of the current selection; Ctrl+Alt+Up/Down adds a cursor on the line above/below. Each cursor edits independently; ESC collapses to a single cursor.
// [x] 4. Autocomplete + snippets: Provide built-in completions for JavaScript, HTML, and CSS (keywords, identifiers, common snippets) with Tab to accept. Support user-editable snippet files (JSON snippet definitions) that add to the built-ins; Tab cycles through snippet placeholders.
// [x] 5. Code folding: Allow collapsing/expanding of function bodies, braces, and block comments via gutter indicators and shortcuts (Ctrl+Shift+[ / Ctrl+Shift+]). Fold state persists per file for the current session.
// [ ] 6. Minimap: Add a right-edge scroll preview rendering a scaled (1-2px per line) block view of the whole file with the current viewport highlighted; clicking or dragging it scrolls the editor. Toggleable.
// [ ] 7. Linter/diagnostics panel: Detect JavaScript syntax errors live as you type (debounced ~400ms) and surface them in a Problems panel grouped by file with line numbers and messages, plus a badge count on the tab; clicking an entry jumps to the line. Show error markers in the editor gutter/line.
// [ ] 8. Find & replace with regex: Implement Find in the active file (match highlighting, next/prev, replace one/all) and Find in Workspace across all files (results grouped by file with match counts; click to jump). Regex mode toggle applies to both.
// [ ] 9. AI code assistant: Add a chat panel powered by generateText that can explain, fix, or generate code and propose edits to the open file as a diff the user can apply or reject. Stream responses with an animated loading indicator.
// [ ] 10. Git-style version history: Snapshot every file on save (kv-backed, keyed per file). Provide a timeline to browse past versions, restore any snapshot, and diff any snapshot against the current content in a side-by-side view. Keep a per-file cap (e.g. 50 snapshots) to bound storage.

// Phase 2: Files & Workspace
// [ ] 11. Import/export zip: Add download of the entire workspace as a single .zip and upload of a .zip to restore it (extract files and folders, merging with existing content). Report clear errors for malformed archives.
// [ ] 12. Share via link: Serialize the workspace into a shareable URL (compressed); for workspaces too large for a URL, use an editable upload and embed its URL. Anyone opening the link sees the workspace restored (read-only).
// [ ] 13. Drag & drop: Support dragging files and folders in the file tree to reorder them within a folder or move them into another folder (drop targets highlight). Also support dragging a file's reordering inside its current folder.
// [ ] 14. Duplicate file & terminal expansion: Add "Duplicate" to the file context menu (creates "<name> copy.ext" in the same folder). Expand the terminal command set beyond the current 13 with cp, mv, grep, find, head, and tail supporting common flags, matching the existing command UX.
// [ ] 15. Compare files: Add a side-by-side diff view comparing two open files: choose the second file from the tree, then show added/removed/changed line highlighting with navigation between differences.

// Phase 3: Perchance Integration
// [ ] 16. Edit your own generator: Add a one-click button that loads this generator's real main.pjs and index.html into the editor as editable files (scratchpad mode). Saving edits writes them back to the live generator; show an explicit indicator of edit/save state.

// Phase 4: UI & Polish
// [ ] 17. Split editors: Support side-by-side editors ("Split Right") for two files: an adjustable divider, independent cursors and undo per pane, and the ability to close a split.
// [ ] 18. Breadcrumbs: Show a path trail (folder/file chain) above the editor that follows the active file; clicking any segment jumps to that file or folder.
// [ ] 19. More themes: Add light and high-contrast presets alongside the existing dark theme, plus an accent color picker. The theme affects editor chrome and syntax colors and persists across sessions.
// [ ] 20. Custom keybindings: Add an editable keybindings.json that remaps command-palette actions; ship the default bindings as a reference and let user overrides take precedence over defaults.

$meta
  title = Code — VS Code-style Editor in Your Browser
  description = A VS Code-style code editor that runs entirely in your browser: virtual file tree, syntax highlighting, a terminal, command palette, search, and a JavaScript runner. Your files persist across reloads.
  tags = code editor, vscode, terminal, javascript, tools
  header
    mode = minimal

kv = {import:kv-plugin}

config
  appName = Code
